te35†Omnidirectional vision , using cite36†360-degree vision to understand the environment, has become increasingly critical across domains like robotics, industrial inspection, and environmental monitoring. Compared to traditional cite37†pinhole vision , cite38†omnidirectional vision provides holistic environmental awareness, significantly enhancing the completeness of scene perception and the reliability of decision-making.\nL92: However, foundational research in this area has historically lagged behind traditional cite37†pinhole vision . This talk presents an emerging trend in the cite39†embodied AI era: the rapid development of omnidirectional vision, driven by growing industrial demand and academic interest. We highlight recent breakthroughs in cite40†omnidirectional generation , cite41†omnidirectional perception , cite42†omnidirectional understanding , and related datasets.\nL93: Drawing on insights from both academia and industry, we propose an ideal cite43†panoramic system architecture in the cite39†embodied AI era, cite44†PANORAMA , which consists of four key subsystems. Moreover, we offer in-depth opinions related to emerging trends and cross-community impacts at the intersection of panoramic vision and embodied AI, along with the future roadmap and open challenges.\nL94: This overview synthesizes state-of-the-art advancements and outlines challenges and opportunities for future research in building robust, general-purpose omnidirectional AI systems in the cite39†embodied AI era.\nL95: cite45†View arXiv page†arxiv.org cite46†View PDF†arxiv.org cite28†Add to collection L96: ### Community\nL97: \nL98: cite29†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L99: \nL100: cite26†Chenfei-Liao L101: \nL102: Paper author Paper submitter cite47†Sep 18, 2025 L103: \nL104: This paper presents a draft overview of the emerging field of omnidirectional vision in the context of embodied AI\nL105: \nL106: Reply\nL107: \nL108: cite